  "novel": "A [[spoiler|spoiler]] alert swept through the group as everyone discovered each other's [[annoying|annoying]] [[habits|habit]]. Ted couldn't stop [[correcting|correct]] people's [[grammar|grammar]]. \"It's 'whom,' not 'who,'\" he would say, and everyone would [[cringe|cringe]].\n\nLily [[chewed|chew]] her food [[loudly|loudly]]. Marshall [[sang|sing]] everything he did. \"I'm getting the mail~\" he would [[chant|chant]].\n\nRobin said \"[[literally|literally]]\" when she meant figuratively. Barney used too many [[catchphrases|catchphrase]]. Each discovery was a [[shock|shock]]. \"How did I never [[notice|notice]] this?\" Ted asked.\n\nThe habits [[bothered|bother]] them at first, but they [[realized|realize]] something important: the people you love were full of [[flaws|flaw]]. You either [[accepted|accept]] them or let them [[ruin|ruin]] everything. They chose to accept.",
